    "id": "e2eff51a-f9c8-47b6-a0c6-6fd51c0b7636",
    "body": "Hint: Use the Second Derivative Test. Once you find the partials $f_{xx}$, $f_{yy}$, and $f_{xy}$, calculate the determinant $D = f_{xx}f_{yy} - (f_{xy})^2$.If $D < 0$, it's a saddle point.If $D > 0$, look at the sign of $f_{xx}$ to decide if it's a max or min.",
